        <body>
            <div xml:id="d708">

                <pb facs="0699" n="583" xml:id="pg583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 365.117/224.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador Page</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 253.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 7, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    telegram No. 351, of October 14, 1915, concerning the detention of Giacomo
                    Carmine Mazza for military service, the Department desires that you report
                    concerning the present status of this matter as soon as the Italian authorities
                    have made a final decision in regard thereto. The father of this person is very
                    anxious to learn whether his son will be released and permitted to return to
                    this country.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
